ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatHopHat = HoP's cap
    .desc = The head of personnel's magnificent, stylish cap.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatCake = cake hat
    .desc = You put the cake on your head. Brilliant.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatChickenhead = chicken head
    .desc = It's a chicken head. Bok bok bok!
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatChef = chef's hat
    .desc = It's a hat used by chefs to keep hair out of your food. Judging by the food in the mess, they don't work.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatWizardFake = fake wizard hat
    .desc = It has WIZZARD written across it in sequins. Comes with a cool beard.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatBraided = braided sunhat
    .desc = A small braided hat for sunny summer days.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatCardborg = cardborg helmet
    .desc = A hat made out of a box.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatCaptainBicorn = captain's bicorne
    .desc = Why be king when you can be emperor?
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatNiko = not-a-cat hat
    .desc = A big brown hat. You only get one shot. It smells of gyros and feta cheese.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatElf = elf hat
    .desc = Santa's little helper's hat.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatFestiveHatGreen = festive green hat
    .desc = Festive headwear to get you in the holiday spirit.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadDemonicHornsDeer = demonic deer horns
    .desc = The horns of the radio demon. Brrr...
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatHelmetVenerator = venerator headpiece
    .desc = A golden halo of rays, the light of Christ. Strangely, it gives off no light at all.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatReindeer = reindeer headband
    .desc = A festive antlered headband to get you in the holiday spirit.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadFloatingFloraCrown = floating flora crown
    .desc = A crown of floating flowers! Isn't that neat?
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatPrincess = princess hat
    .desc = A tall pink cone hat with a golden streamer at the tip. Did you know these are actually called hennins?
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatWitch1 = witch hat
    .desc = A witch's hat.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatWideBrimmed = wide-brimmed sunhat
    .desc = A wide-brimmed summer hat, perfect for sunny days. But where would a space station get those?
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadBeretSquadCharlie = beret with purple badge
    .desc = A dark grey beret with a small purple badge on the side. It looks military, but pairs surprisingly well with a lab coat.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatTVHead = TV head
    .desc = An old boxy television worn over the head, its cord dangling behind. The label says it will make you look like a true Tumblr sexyman, whatever that means.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatStrawHatWide = wide straw hat
    .desc = A wide-brimmed straw hat with a blue ribbon. Makes you look mysterious.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadOfficerBeret = black officer's beret
    .desc = A black beret with a silver badge on the side. Officers wear it at a rakish angle to look sharp on patrol.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatFedoraBrown = brown fedora
    .desc = It's a brown fedora.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatHopcap = head of personnel's dress cap
    .desc = A grand, stylish head of personnel's cap.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatBeretHoS = head of security's beret
    .desc = A black beret with a commander's rank emblem. For officers that are more inclined towards style than safety.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatHoshat = head of security's cap
    .desc = The robust standard-issue cap of the head of security. For showing the officers who's in charge.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatCapcap = captain's cap
    .desc = A grand, stylish cap worn by the captain. Shows the station who's in charge.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatWizard = wizard hat
    .desc = A strange-looking blue hat that most certainly belonged to a powerful magic-user.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatWideBrimmedBlack = black wide-brimmed hat
    .desc = An elegant wide-brimmed summer hat, perfect for mourning.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadShamanSkull = shaman skull
    .desc = The bleached skull of a horned beast, worn as a headdress. Its empty eye sockets stare at everyone you meet.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatSecurityTrooper = trooper hat
    .desc = A campaign hat for NT troopers. It originally came with a case, but you lost it.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatTrapperBlack = black trapper hat
    .desc = A black trapper hat with fluffy fur flaps.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatTrapperGray = grey trapper hat
    .desc = A grey trapper hat with fluffy fur flaps.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadBeretASO = support officer's beret
    .desc = A black beret with a badge, as worn by Auxiliary Support Officers.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadCapSPPPolBlack = commissar's peaked cap
    .desc = A black peaked cap issued to political commissars of all stripes. It reminds you of October.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadHatNTNCGrey = grey naval cap
    .desc = A grey Nanotrasen navy marine cap with a black visor.
